# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 07-overrides-legal

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

STANDARD OVERRIDES — ACCEPTED DEVIATIONS PER PRODUCT
(BINDING)

\================================================================================



Principle

\- The global standard stays strict; a product may
document an intentional, accepted deviation

  without
weakening the family bar for other apps.

\- Overrides are explicit, reviewable, and persistent
until revoked — not silent exceptions in verify scripts.



Registry (required for shipped products)

\- File:
Desktop/Nivo78/Common/standard-overrides/{ProductCode}.overrides.json (APA:
{ProductCode}.overrides.json)

\- Rule ids: reference/NIVO78\_STANDARD\_RULE\_IDS.txt —
add new ids before referencing them

\- README: reference/standard-overrides/README.txt
(schema); Desktop/Nivo78/Common/standard-overrides/README.txt (location)



Override entry (required fields)

\- override\_id — stable id for later edits (manage
script generates on -Add)

\- rule\_id   —
stable id from NIVO78\_STANDARD\_RULE\_IDS.txt

\- surface   —
website | app | kb | audit | tooling | all

\- scope     —
repo-relative path or functional area

\- reason    —
plain-language justification (min 10 characters)

\- accepted  —
ISO date YYYY-MM-DD

\- status    —
active | revoked



Optional: detail (sub-scope), updated (auto on
change), review\_by (warn when passed), ticket,

owner, compensating\_control, risk (see Override
governance / APP-OVERRIDE-\*)



Edit workflow

\- tools/maintain/manage-standard-overrides.ps1 — list,
show, add, update, revoke, reactivate (-OverrideId)

\- Change reason, scope, review date, or status with
-Update; do not hand-edit JSON unless necessary

\- Revoke when fixed; -Reactivate if waiver needed
again



Never waivable

\- Silent data upload, silent diagnostics, background
bug reporting

\- Breadcrumb / UI-event ring buffer or
attachBreadcrumbsToBugReport in any release / main source set

\- Secrets shown on screen after save, skipping vault
encryption where required

\- Pre-checked legal acceptance or core workflows
without terms acknowledgement

\- Intentional security bypasses in release (debug
unlocks, test credentials, development endpoints)



Override governance (APP-OVERRIDE-\* — see OVERRIDE
GOVERNANCE section)

\- Active overrides should record approving owner and
compensating control where applicable (APP-OVERRIDE-OWNER).

\- Active overrides should set review\_by (date or
trigger) and must not become permanent by neglect (APP-OVERRIDE-REVIEW).

\- Overrides that weaken security, privacy, integrity,
or release controls should record risk (APP-OVERRIDE-RISK).

\- Revoke when no longer needed (APP-OVERRIDE-CLEANUP).
Optional registry fields: owner, compensating\_control, risk.



Tooling contract

\- tools/maintain/manage-standard-overrides.ps1 — list,
add, update, revoke, reactivate overrides by override\_id

\- tools/lib/N78StandardOverrides.ps1 — load and match
overrides

\- tools/verify/verify-standard-overrides.ps1 —
validate registry (release gate)

\- tools/verify/verify-apa-website.ps1 — skip failing
checks covered by active overrides; log ACCEPTED

\- Marketing drift checks honor MARKETING-HUB-\*
overrides with detail matching the bullet warning



Text tests (Nivo78 app.txt vector STANDARD-OVERRIDES)

\- Load
Desktop/Nivo78/Common/standard-overrides/{ProductCode}.overrides.json before
scoring

\- Finding matches active override (rule\_id + surface +
scope) → report ACCEPTED-OVERRIDE with reason; not FAIL

\- Violation with no override → normal finding severity

\- Flag: unknown rule\_id, missing reason, expired
review\_by still active, orphaned override with no matching check

\- App audit vectors (APP-\*) and audit-vector waivers
apply to manual/code review findings



Workflow

\- When you accept a deviation for the product you are
working on, add or update the override in the same change

  — do not
disable verify scripts globally.

\- Revoke (status revoked) when the product is brought
back into compliance.





