DIAGNOSTICS ON BUG REPORTS — USER PERMISSION REQUIRED

\================================================================================



Principle

\- Diagnostics help support reproduce issues; they are
never collected silently or uploaded in the background.

\- The user sees what will be included, toggles
optional extras, and reviews the full draft before send.



Always included in bug reports (minimal operational
snapshot)

\- App name and version

\- Host OS summary (e.g. Windows 11, Android 14 — no
raw env dumps)

\- Active screen or destination id (which page the user
was on)

\- Product-neutral progress flags only when relevant
(e.g. checklist counts — not business record contents)



Included by default; user can turn off extended block
(bug reports; optional on Feedback comments when offered)

\- Checkbox: “Attach extra troubleshooting details” —
shown for Bug report (default ON) and optionally Feedback comments (default
OFF); never on Feature request; plain explanation of what that means.

\- Feature request: no extended diagnostics checkbox —
contact and narrative only.

\- Extended block may include: recent sign-in or
security audit lines (timestamps and action labels only), tier or mode labels,
schema versions — whatever helps support without exposing business data.

\- Bug reports MUST always include minimal
SETTINGS\_FOR\_SUPPORT even when extended checkbox is OFF; extended audit block
still applies for bug reports per product composer policy (user sees draft
before send).

\- How-to questions MUST NOT be a Feedback report type
— use the Help hub.



Debug-only breadcrumb snapshot
(APP-BREADCRUMB-DEBUG-ONLY)

\- Every Nivo78 app MUST implement the shared
10,000-event breadcrumb ring buffer (nivo78-breadcrumbs

  or an
equivalent Clean Engine copy) with expect/actual \`isDebugBuild\` and
\`MutexLock\`.

\- \`log(event)\` MUST begin with \`if (!isDebugBuild)
return\`. \`getSnapshot()\` MUST return

  \`Release Build
\- No Logs\` when \`isDebugBuild\` is false.

\- Text input MUST log action + character count only —
never the typed value.

\- \`attachBreadcrumbsToBugReport\` MUST live only in the
debug source set (\`src/androidDebug/kotlin\`

  for KMP
libraries, \`src/debug/kotlin\` for Android apps). Never \`src/androidMain\`,
\`src/main\`,

  or
\`src/release\`.

\- Full 10,000-event dumps are a local debug file, not
mailto. A short debug tail MAY appear in

  extended
diagnostics on debug builds only.

\- Release binaries MUST NOT allocate the ring buffer
and MUST NOT include the export utility.



Never include without explicit user paste

\- Passwords, tokens, API keys, vault contents

\- Full file paths to user projects (redact to basename
or remove)

\- Bank, tax, government, or payout identifiers

\- Email bodies, customer lists, or exported
attachments

\- Database files or project folder trees



Redaction rules (engine-side, before mailto)

\- Run diagnostics through a privacy redactor: strip
path prefixes, token-like strings, and fields on a deny list.

\- Copy on the Feedback page states plainly: “Bug
reports include app version and which page you were on. Optional details
exclude project folders and saved passwords. Do not paste secrets unless you
choose to.”

\- When extended diagnostics is OFF, send the minimal
snapshot only; do not sneak extended fields into the body.



Platform limits

\- Respect mailto URL length limits (especially
Windows); truncate or summarize with a note in the draft when necessary — never
fail silently.





\================================================================================

LEGAL GATING AND CUSTOMER ACKNOWLEDGEMENT — EVERY APP

\================================================================================



Principle

\- Users must explicitly agree to Terms and acknowledge
Privacy before core workflows — no silent acceptance, no pre-checked boxes, no
bypass on upgrade unless terms version unchanged.

\- Legal copy lives in engine-layer registries (product
equivalent of ApaLegalCopy, ApaDataSecurityCopy) — not scattered in
Composables.

\- First-run dialog, menu Privacy/Terms links, and
in-repo privacy/terms HTML must tell the same story.



Explicit consent (first run and re-consent)

\- Modal first-run legal dialog blocks the core shell
until the user accepts or declines.

\- Acceptance checkbox defaults unchecked; Accept
button disabled until checked.

\- Full Terms and Privacy reachable from the dialog
before accepting — stable URLs (nivo78.com/{product}/…) or equivalent in-app
viewers.

\- No silent acceptance on install, upgrade, or terms
bump.

\- Plain-language in-app summary in the dialog; full
policy on linked pages (layered disclosure).



Decline integrity

\- Decline button label must match behavior on every
platform (desktop, mobile, tablet).

\- If copy says “Decline and exit” (or equivalent), the
app exits or fully blocks core workflows — not a no-op with full access.

\- If the product allows limited use without
acceptance, relabel the button honestly — never promise exit while leaving
workflows open.



Versioned acceptance record

\- Record acceptance in engine/support layer with:
terms version, timestamp, app version at accept time.

\- Single gateway API per product (product equivalent
of ApaLegalAcceptanceGateway) — platform stores implement persistence.

\- When TERMS\_VERSION (or product equivalent)
increases, users who accepted an older version see the first-run dialog again.

\- Privacy policy documents what the acceptance record
contains and where it is stored on device.



Startup legal gate

\- Core workflows unreachable before acceptance:
open/create primary workspace, setup checklists, export/handoff, vault unlock
when product policy requires legal gate first.

\- Document and keep consistent the order of legal gate
vs master-password or vault setup on each platform.

\- Menu Privacy and Terms remain reachable after
acceptance — not only on first run.



Legal copy accuracy (aligned with privacy/terms web
pages)

\- In-app Terms privacy summary matches engine security
copy and code/Website privacy HTML (plain vs encrypted vs blocked vs never
stored).

\- Terms state: not legal, tax, or store advice; no
store affiliation or guaranteed approval outcomes.

\- Platform scope honest in Terms, Privacy, and support
pages (desktop vs companion vs unsupported form factors).

\- Optional third-party egress (e.g. user-configured AI
API) disclosed in Terms/Privacy when shipped — user-initiated only.



Cross-platform parity

\- Same TERMS\_VERSION and first-run dialog copy on
desktop, mobile, and tablet shells.

\- Decline, accept, and re-consent behavior equivalent
across platforms; document intentional storage-path differences in privacy
policy only.



Store and entity alignment

\- In-repo and hosted privacy/terms URLs match Partner
Center / Play Console / App Store Connect listing requirements.

\- Legal entity name consistent: Nivo78 Mobile Apps,
LLC (or successor named in Terms) across Terms, Privacy, support, and in-app copy.



Audit and ship

\- Run reference/text-tests-audit/prompts/Legal.txt
when consent, terms version, or legal copy changes.

\- Run updocs after ApaLegalCopy (or product
equivalent) or privacy/terms HTML changes.





